  "adjustment_changelog": [
    {
      "date": "2026-07-28",
      "who": "owner",
      "what": "Initial knobs, one config for all three recipes (the recipe is the only experimental variable): LoRA r=16 alpha=32, attn+MLP target modules, lr 2e-4 linear, 3 epochs with per-epoch checkpoints, batch 32x1, max_seq_len 256, completion-only loss.",
      "why": "r=16/alpha=32 = the light end of the coached range (small data, 27 classes); attn+MLP over attn-only for capacity headroom; lr at the top of the 1e-4..2e-4 range since LoRA tolerates it; epochs=3 with per-epoch VAL sweep so the epoch count is a measurement, not a guess; seq 256 sized to recipe B's ~p95 chat-templated length from the dry-run stats."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-28",
      "who": "agent (engineering, not hyperparameters)",
      "what": "Two Windows-stack workarounds, no training-math changes: (1) --stage runs one epoch per process with HF checkpoint resume, plus a gc+empty_cache flush every 50 steps, to dodge a VRAM-creep livelock that reproduces past ~350 optimizer steps per process; (2) recipe B inference decodes free-form first and constrained-re-decodes only schema failures, because LMFE per-token enforcement is ~100x slower inside free-text rationale fields.",
      "why": "Documented in docs/ENV-4090-WINDOWS.md; optimizer/scheduler/RNG are restored on resume so a staged run is the same training run."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-28",
      "who": "owner",
      "what": "No mid-run hyperparameter adjustments were made; the initial config ran to completion for all three recipes.",
      "why": "First pass intentionally identical across recipes; tuning would fork the controlled comparison."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-28",
      "who": "agent (post-run audit, verified in trainer_log_recipe_a.jsonl)",
      "what": "Found and fixed a --stage flaw: each stage process rebuilt the LR scheduler with num_train_epochs=stage, so the decay total was per-stage, not per-run. Bitext recipe_a (the only staged run, 3 stages) trained under an unintended warm-restart sawtooth - linear 2e-4->0 within epoch 1, then 1e-4->0, then 6.9e-5->0 - instead of one linear decay over 537 steps. Fix: the schedule is now always built for the full run and a callback halts the process at the stage boundary, so staged == unstaged.",
      "why": "The lr column in the trainer log shows LR hitting ~0 at steps 180/358/537 and jumping back up after each resume. ablation and recipe_b fit in one process and are unaffected."
    }
  ],
  "caveats": [
